  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Plotting the graph of the given functions, we get the shaded region as the area bounded by the curves.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/dec5b7b5-87ca-4f94-9315-a2e4e2392e1c-image.png\" style=\"width: 289px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p>Given, area of shaded region <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>364</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>364</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>364</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>364</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>729</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
